Subject: [PATCH 11146/11171] [outer-loop] Resolve no-LLM alias members
 structurally (SCENARIO-SUBSTRATE-ALIAS-1-B)

First of the three triaged audit findings. The guard asked whether a diff adds
a quoted *_no_llm string. The tuple is not written that way: of 53 members, 32
are constant names, 1 is a starred tuple, and 20 are bare literals. So it
covered a minority of the shapes in use and the normal way to add an alias --
define a constant, name it in the tuple -- produced no matching literal and
walked through.

The named missed input resolves to a value that does not end in _no_llm at all,
so widening the regex would not have caught it either. The fix reads the tuple
from the staged and HEAD sources with ast and diffs the resolved values,
expanding constant names and starred tuples. The literal scan is kept because
it also catches an alias added outside the tuple.

Mutation result stated honestly: 2 of 3 RED. The third deleted an empty-staged
early return and the suite stayed green, proving that branch decorative, since
the empty set minus anything is already empty. Removed rather than left to read
as protection. That is the discipline's own instruction applied to my own code.

Verified the widened lint exits 0 against the current repo, so it does not
retroactively refuse the existing tuple.

